---
const title = "Court deadline control, automated — Facundo Sarina";
const description =
  "A case study: reading a court filing portal to find the procedural obligations a law firm had missed. 404 cases audited, 11 overdue items found.";

const stats = [
  { n: "404", l: "active cases audited in one run" },
  { n: "11", l: "overdue obligations found, across 7 cases" },
  { n: "13", l: "judicial districts covered" },
  { n: "~1,300", l: "lines of Python, with tests" },
];

const checks = [
  "Complaint served, but the corresponding notice never filed",
  "Evidence stage opened without the letters or notices it requires",
  "A letter or notice ordered in the ruling and never sent",
  "Court fees ordered but not credited",
  "A letter or notice rejected by the court and never refiled",
];

const states = [
  {
    k: "Missing",
    d: "No filing by the firm cites that ruling. If another party filed one, the report says so.",
  },
  {
    k: "Awaiting court signature",
    d: "The firm filed it; the court has not countersigned yet. Nothing to do but wait.",
  },
  {
    k: "Needs review",
    d: "A letter went out, but not to every recipient the ruling named. A human has to look.",
  },
  {
    k: "Could not be checked",
    d: "The run could not read these. They carry over to the next one.",
  },
];

const sample = [
  { date: "02/10/2024", mov: "Letter ordered", missing: "Letter never filed", days: 28 },
  { date: "19/09/2024", mov: "Evidence stage opened", missing: "Notice to defendant", days: 41 },
  { date: "11/09/2024", mov: "Fees ordered", missing: "Court fee not credited", days: 49 },
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Court deadline control, automated" />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <main>
      <header class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Case study · Legal operations</p>
        <h1>Court deadline control, automated</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Estudio Pantuso y Asociados, a labour-law firm in Quilmes, Buenos Aires, was checking
          procedural deadlines by hand, case by case, and it had stopped scaling. I built a system
          that reads the court's filing portal and works out what the firm still owes. In its
          largest run it went through <strong>404 active cases</strong> and found{" "}
          <strong>11 overdue obligations across 7 of them</strong>.
        </p>
      </header>

      <ul class="stats">
        {
          stats.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <span class="n">{s.n}</span>
              <span class="l">{s.l}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <section>
        <h2>The problem</h2>
        <p>
          In Argentine labour litigation, every ruling a court issues creates obligations for the
          parties: serve process, file a letter to an outside body, pay a fee. Miss one and the case
          stalls — or worse. There is no reminder; it is on the firm to notice.
        </p>
        <p>
          I have handled case management at this firm since 2018 — workplace-injury and occupational
          illness claims, around thirty filings a week — so the gap was mine before it was a
          project. The method was to open each case in the court portal and read its history. With
          several hundred active cases spread across thirteen judicial districts, that check got
          done when someone had time, which is to say not reliably.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The hard part is not reading the portal</h2>
        <p>
          Scraping the case history is the easy half. The real question is harder:{" "}
          <em>has this obligation been met or not?</em> A ruling orders a notice; weeks later some
          document appears in the file. Is it the right one?
        </p>
        <p>
          So the system links every filing back to the ruling that ordered it. For each letter or
          notice it opens the document and reads four things: who signed it, who it is addressed to,
          which ruling date it cites, and whether the court has countersigned. A ruling counts as
          complied with <strong>only</strong> when there is a filing by this firm citing that
          ruling's date. Anything still open after ten days is flagged.
        </p>
        <h3>What it looks for</h3>
        <ul class="checks">
          {checks.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Four states, not two</h2>
        <p>
          An early version answered "done" or "missing" and was wrong often enough to be useless.
          Court workflows have middle states, and a deadline tool that hides them trains people to
          ignore it. The report has four:
        </p>
        <dl class="states">
          {
            states.map((s) => (
              <div>
                <dt>{s.k}</dt>
                <dd>{s.d}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <p class="aside">
          The fourth matters most. If a run cannot read twenty cases, a report that quietly leaves
          them out reads as "all clear" — which is exactly the failure a deadline tool exists to
          prevent. Unreadable cases are listed by name and carried to the next run.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What came out</h2>
        <p>
          One email a day, only when something was overdue. If nothing was, it sent nothing. If it
          could not reach the portal at all, it said so rather than reporting silence as good news.
        </p>

        <figure class="report">
          <figcaption>Sample output — anonymised, real layout</figcaption>
          <div class="report-head">
            <strong>Overdue filings — 02/10/2026</strong>
            <span>11 pending across 7 cases, out of 404 checked</span>
          </div>
          <div class="case">
            <p class="case-name">CASE NAME REDACTED — claim for damages</p>
            <p class="case-meta">File 00000 · Labour Court No. 2 · open</p>
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Ruling date</th><th>What it ordered</th><th>What is missing</th><th>Days</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {
                  sample.map((r) => (
                    <tr>
                      <td>{r.date}</td>
                      <td>{r.mov}</td>
                      <td>{r.missing}</td>
                      <td class="days">{r.days}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))
                }
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Engineering decisions worth naming</h2>
        <dl class="states">
          <div>
            <dt>It backs off instead of pushing through</dt>
            <dd>
              When the portal asks for a security check, the script stops, waits — up to an hour —
              and resumes more slowly, thirty seconds between pages. It never attempts to work
              around the check. A tool that gets the firm's account flagged is worse than no tool.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>It only re-reads what changed</dt>
            <dd>
              Rulings are cached, and cases with no movement for over a year are skipped. Each run
              does the smallest amount of reading that still gives a correct answer.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>The matching rules are tested</dt>
            <dd>
              The logic that decides "complied with" is the part that must not be wrong, so it sits
              in its own module with its own tests, separate from the scraping.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <footer>
        <p class="stack">
          <strong>Stack</strong> · Python · Playwright · BeautifulSoup · HTML reporting · SMTP
        </p>
        <p class="who">
          Facundo Sarina — legal operations and process automation.{" "}
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/facundo-sarina">LinkedIn</a> ·{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/facundosarina">GitHub</a>
        </p>
        <p class="note">
          Built and run during 2026 at Estudio Pantuso y Asociados, where I have handled case
          management since 2018. No client data appears on this page: the sample report reproduces
          the real layout with invented content.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    --ground: #ffffff;
    --surface: #f6f8f8;
    --line: #dde4e5;
    --ink: #1a1a1a;
    --muted: #55605f;
    --accent: #0e5f66;
    --warn: #8a5a12;
    --warn-soft: #fbf1dd;
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --ground: #101618;
      --surface: #182022;
      --line: #2b3639;
      --ink: #e6edee;
      --muted: #9aa8aa;
      --accent: #4cc0ca;
      --warn: #e0b061;
      --warn-soft: #30260f;
    }
  }

  :root[data-theme="dark"] {
    --ground: #101618;
    --surface: #182022;
    --line: #2b3639;
    --ink: #e6edee;
    --muted: #9aa8aa;
    --accent: #4cc0ca;
    --warn: #e0b061;
    --warn-soft: #30260f;
  }

  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--ground);
    color: var(--ink);
    font: 17px/1.65 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
  }

  main {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 16px 5rem;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 2.8rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    margin: 0.2em 0 0.4em;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 3rem 0 0.8rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.6rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 1.05em;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.14rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .lede strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .stats {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(9rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .stats li {
    background: var(--ground);
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
  }

  .stats .n {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .stats .l {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
  }

  .checks {
    margin: 0 0 1em;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
  }

  .checks li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4em;
  }

  .states {
    margin: 1.2rem 0 1.4rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .states > div {
    background: var(--ground);
    padding: 0.95rem 1.1rem;
  }

  .states dt {
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }

  .states dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .aside {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
  }

  .report {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .report figcaption {
    padding: 0.55rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .report-head {
    padding: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .report-head strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .report-head span {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .case {
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .case-name {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 650;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .case-meta {
    margin: 0.1rem 0 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  th {
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem 0.35rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  td {
    padding: 0.5rem 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .days {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--warn);
    background: var(--warn-soft);
    text-align: center;
    width: 3.2rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  footer {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  footer .stack strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  footer a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  footer .note {
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    main {
      padding-top: 2.5rem;
    }
    table {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
    }
  }
</style>
